From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: YanIanZ <iwayanbagusaryadarma@student.telkomuniversity.ac.id>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 02:03:18 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] SourbyCraft - ServerTickManager is supported

The tick manager is implemented server-wide (ServerTickControl), so the
@Unsupported marker goes; the javadoc states how the state applies to
regions.

diff --git a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/ServerTickManager.java b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/ServerTickManager.java
index 86ad1c75f3992e067395cba76b09b9e6d144349f..8756da3e4fff73cec078156f76f6c9116186f7a4 100644
--- a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/ServerTickManager.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/ServerTickManager.java
@@ -2,16 +2,21 @@ package org.bukkit;
 
 import org.bukkit.entity.Entity;
 import org.jetbrains.annotations.NotNull;
-import dev.iyanz.sourbycraft.api.Unsupported;
 
 /**
  * Manages ticking within a server.
  * <p>
  * To learn more about the features surrounding this interface.
  *
+ * <p>
+ * SourbyCraft: the state applies to every region and the global tick. Changes may be requested
+ * from any thread and take effect at the next global tick; each region observes them at the start
+ * of its own next tick, so regions are not frozen at one shared tick boundary. Stepping and
+ * sprinting count global ticks. A region's own pause/sprint
+ * ({@code Server#getRegionThreadingTickRateManager()}) is separate and still applies.
+ *
  * @see <a href="https://minecraft.wiki/w/Commands/tick">Tick Command</a>
  */
-@Unsupported // Canvas - region threading
 public interface ServerTickManager {
 
     /**
